During the CMake bootstrap stage the GHS generator sources are not
compiled, and the only GHS use in cmake.cxx is already guarded by
!defined(CMAKE_BOOTSTRAP). However the header is included unconditionally
on Linux/Windows hosts, and its inline cmGlobalGhsMultiGenerator::NewFactory()
constructs cmGlobalGeneratorSimpleFactory<cmGlobalGhsMultiGenerator>. Host
GCC 16 emits that factory's vtable into cmake.o just from the include,
pulling in undefined references to the GHS constructor and GetDocumentation()
and breaking the bootstrap link. Guard the include with !CMAKE_BOOTSTRAP so
no GHS symbols are referenced during bootstrap.

--- a/Source/cmake.cxx
+++ b/Source/cmake.cxx
@@ -130,7 +130,7 @@

 // NOTE: the __linux__ macro is predefined on Android host too, but
 // main CMakeLists.txt filters out this generator by host name.
-#if (defined(__linux__) && !defined(__ANDROID__)) || defined(_WIN32)
+#if !defined(CMAKE_BOOTSTRAP) && ((defined(__linux__) && !defined(__ANDROID__)) || defined(_WIN32))
 #  include "cmGlobalGhsMultiGenerator.h"
 #endif
